      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Little Ossipee River supplies Lake Arrowhead’s surface inflows, entering from Balch Pond and unnamed tributaries draining nearby wetlands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lake_arrowhead_maine",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In spring, snowmelt from the region’s average 67 inches of snowfall can raise lake levels by several feet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lake_arrowhead_maine",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lake Arrowhead served as a filming location for the TV series “Murder, She Wrote,” where many outdoor scenes were shot on its shores.",
